            "text": "{\"primary_meaning\":\"The Word of God, functioning as a spiritual weapon of truth that convicts the heart, exposes inner thoughts, and defeats spiritual opposition.\",\"primary_basis\":[\"Ephesians 6:17\",\"Hebrews 4:12\",\"Revelation 1:16\",\"Revelation 19:15\"],\"alternatives\":[{\"meaning\":\"Divine judgment, wrath, and military destruction\",\"basis\":[\"Isaiah 34:5\",\"Ezekiel 21:9-10\",\"Revelation 6:4\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"Earthly authority, governmental justice, and the power of the state to execute punishment\",\"basis\":[\"Romans 13:4\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"Division, ideological conflict, or relational strife provoked by the Gospel\",\"basis\":[\"Matthew 10:34\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"}],\"has_settled_consensus\":true,\"confidence\":\"high\",\"notes\":\"The sword has a highly settled consensus in Christian interpretation that depends largely on its contextual category: in spiritual warfare contexts it universally represents the Word of God; in civic contexts it represents government authority; and in eschatological or prophetic contexts it represents judgment or division.\"}",
